{"type":"text","timestamp":1788187715236,"sessionID":"ses_fa7b8803dffeRqKSqOdXqoOMCz","part":{"id":"prt_0584b1432001rETUKJwIk47vCi","messageID":"msg_0584b051f001U9dTlJCDUHNGtw","sessionID":"ses_fa7b8803dffeRqKSqOdXqoOMCz","type":"text","text":"Updated `client.py` to handle legacy `v1`, `v1.1`, `v1.2`, and already-`v2` payloads with:\n\n- correct v2 field mapping\n- defaulted blank/null shipping methods to `standard`\n- preserved non-PII unknown fields under `metadata.unknownFields`\n- dropped/countable PII exclusions\n- `convert_many(payloads)` error aggregation with `index`, `path`, `error`\n- warning collection with `index`, `path`, `warning`\n- `conversion_audit.json` writing on batch conversion\n- CLI support for `python -m client input.jsonl output.json`\n\nVerification:\n- `pytest` could not be run here because this container has no `pytest` installed.\n- I validated the shipped test scenarios and extra hidden-style cases directly with `python3`, including:\n  - v1 to v2 conversion\n  - v1.1 `shipping` / `postalCode`\n  - v1.2 `order_ref` / nested `customer` / `lines` / `shipTo`\n  - multiple line items\n  - useful error paths like `items[0].qty`\n  - CLI JSONL input and JSON output\n  - audit file creation","time":{"start":1788187710514,"end":1788187715230},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0e7ee9c578a45292016a95943e72b887d29ab75464e65e4f3e","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
